  "final_answer": "I successfully navigated to the Occasions section of Allrecipes and identified holiday recipes sections. The \"Holidays and Events\" subsection under Occasions lists numerous holiday recipe collections. Here are **at least 6 holiday recipes sections** mentioned:\n\n| # | Section Name | URL |\n|---|--------------|-----|\n| 1 | **Easter Recipes** | https://www.allrecipes.com/recipes/85/holidays-and-events/ |\n| 2 | **Halloween Recipes** | https://www.allrecipes.com/recipes/85/holidays-and-events/ |\n| 3 | **Thanksgiving Recipes** | https://www.allrecipes.com/recipes/85/holidays-and-events/ |\n| 4 | **Christmas Recipes** | https://www.allrecipes.com/recipes/85/holidays-and-events/ |\n| 5 | **Hanukkah Recipes** | https://www.allrecipes.com/recipes/85/holidays-and-events/ |\n| 6 | **Tailgating Recipes** | https://www.allrecipes.com/recipes/85/holidays-and-events/ |\n| 7 | **Rosh Hashanah Recipes** | https://www.allrecipes.com/recipes/85/holidays-and-events/ |\n| 8 | **Mardi Gras Recipes** | https://www.allrecipes.com/recipes/85/holidays-and-events/ |\n\nAll of these are listed under the **\"Holidays and Events\"** subsection of the **Occasions** menu on Allrecipes.com, with the page description: *\"Celebrate with top-rated holiday cookies, appetizers, and desserts. Find the right recipe for any holiday.\"*\n\nAdditional holiday sections available on the same page (off-screen but visible in the navigation) include: Mother's Day, Memorial Day, Cinco de Mayo, New Year's, Big Game, Veteran's Day, 4th of July, Kwanzaa, Passover, Ramadan, St. Patrick's Day, Diwali, Lunar New Year, Purim, Holiday Planning, Back to School, Christmas Cookies, April Fools' Day, and Oktoberfest Recipes — well exceeding the 6 minimum requested.",
